      "gap": "Account for every evidence claim in the selected source extent and fix the finite dependent-source set before authoring those claims: the body (handbook/parts/p15/rationality-5-3.tex) does not account for the chapter's evidence/attribution claims about (a) Benferhat, Bonnefon and Da Silva Neves (2005) empirical tests of possibilistic default reasoning (p.342); (b) Eichhorn, Kern-Isberner and Ragni (2018) conditional-logical ranking model for elaborating plausible background knowledge (pp.342-343); (c) the indirect route of testing ranking theory via its parallels to probability theory, citing Henrion, Provan, Del Favero and Sanders (1994) (p.343); (d) Colombo, Elkin and Hartmann (2018) on the Bayesian boom neglecting alternative frameworks such as ranking theory (p.342); (e) the independence properties for advanced belief revision of Jin and Thielscher (2007) and Delgrande and Jin (2012) related to ranking independence via Spohn (2012, ch.7) and Kern-Isberner and Huvermann (2017) (p.342; only 'later multiple-change approaches' at body l.557-558); (f) Levi and Harper identities and Kern-Isberner, Bock, Sauerwald and Beierle (2017) showing iterated revision and contraction performed by a common methodology (p.342); (g) the claim that Dempster-Shafer theory comprises probability and ranking theory as special cases and that the divergent dynamics preventing reduction are argued in Spohn (2012, sec. 11.9) (p.341; body l.495-498 states only the static consonant equivalence); (h) the stability-theory proposals of Leitgeb (2017) and Raidl and Skovgaard-Olsen (2017) as the unresolved probability-belief bridge (p.341); and no explicit finite dependent-source set is declared (body l.714-716 names the 2014 model and 2017/2019 work without fixing which dependent sources are opened and which claims rest only on the chapter's attribution).",
